  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1108 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nQuiet weather and a steady warming trend remain the main highlights \nof the extended period. Highs will eventually reach the 60s and even \nlower 70s for some places by the end of the workweek. A broad upper \nlevel trough look to overtake the Great Plains by the midweek, \nbut forcing seems to be lackluster over our CWA for any \nprecipitation to occur at this time. A second upper level trough \nwill traverse across the Plains by Friday, and long range models \nare more keen on introducing PoPs on Friday due to better quality \nmoisture profiles across the Panhandles and a more favorable\npotential track of the upper low.\n\nRangel",
